        "summary": "Two data sources agree it’s more likely to pass than fail. Across 10 local RCV votes, a city as Democratic as Irvine (Harris 61% of the two-party vote) would be expected to give about 54% Yes. Irvine’s own last vote on how its council is elected (2024 Measure D) passed with 59.8%. Averaging the two gives about 57%, with about a 78% chance of passing.",
